                <pb facs="0957" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/844: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-21T08:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                                1919, 8 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            August 24.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Resignation of Federico Tinoco was presented to his Congress yesterday afternoon
                    by Quiros who was named by it for the balance of the term. Extra session then
                    declared ended. I am arranging for meeting to comply with the instructions by
                    cable August 19th, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
